Slide sorter accessibles: take the SolarMutex before the disposed check.

AccessibleSlideSorterObject and AccessibleSlideSorterView checked ensureAlive()/ThrowIfDisposed()
and only then took the SolarMutex (getAccessibleChildCount/getAccessibleChild of the view took no
SolarMutex at all). The gtk3 accessibility bridge calls them from the main loop, which runs with the
SolarMutex released, so a call could pass the check, wait for the SolarMutex held by another thread
that disposes the objects and destroys the slide sorter (Desktop::terminate over UNO), and then use
the destroyed slide sorter: SIGSEGV in SlideSorterModel::GetPageDescriptor /
SlideSorterController::GetPageSelector on HST Draw with AT-SPI active. Locking first makes the check
see the disposal, so the call throws DisposedException, which the bridge handles. Upstream bug
(same code in LibreOffice 26.8.1.1 and 26.8.3.1).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sd_a11y (hst-sd-slidesorter-a11y-dispose-race-test.patch),
tests/runtime/check-draw-a11y-walk-terminate.py.
